# SFT execution status v0.81

2026-09-13. The corrected v2 CPU-qualification successor is prepared locally.
Nothing was committed, pushed, acquired or executed remotely in this stage.
Gate 5 remains incomplete and production eligibility remains false.

## Prepared successor

The v2 workflow uses the existing frozen native harness, supervisor, source
admission and accepted-software hashes. Only publication/provenance bindings,
the private attempt namespace, verifier bindings and corresponding tests are
versioned. Current publication parent `9a4a191fa96753f7d8ae78cedbee54f16d536a04`
is separate from the historical guardian head
`ecc545fc423650bf1089311915290523c10b3172`; both are independently tested.
The portable v1 acquisition-test correction remains the only tracked change.

Preflight now has three independent provider-visible steps: executable hashes,
frozen source admission, then portable pure tests. This localizes a future
failure without reading raw logs. It still cannot prove the exact exception.
No fifth receipt or pre-created acquisition output directory was introduced.
Empty upload success must still not be mistaken for an artifact.

Nine steps have 35 configured phase-minutes and one minute reserve within the
unchanged 36-minute job limit. Source/Spark CI can add 55 aggregate runner-minutes,
so the total configured limit remains 91, not a wall-time or cost prediction.

## Verification and exact publication

191 combined old/new top-level tests pass on Python 3.11.15, 3.13.7 and 3.14.6,
with zero failures/errors/skips. The exact future six-module suite separately
passes 137 top-level tests. Socket/process-start audit hooks blocked external
operations; none were attempted and no ML modules were loaded. The source-only
CLI verifies 57 source files. Ruff and YAML checks pass. These are local
