## External blocker and remaining authority

One attempted read-only refresh of the prior Source CI was rejected before its
command started: the approval system reported workspace credits exhausted.
No HTTP GET was consumed; the historical audit remains at 8/16 GETs used.
There was no bypass or indirect retry. Therefore the prior CI snapshot is not
a current success/failure claim. The workspace owner must restore that prerequisite.

Fresh approval must bind this v0.2 plan before publication or remote execution.
After that, live bounded checks must again confirm private repo, exact remote
parent, no open PR, no active Source/Spark CI and the exact file allowlist.
Any mismatch stops before push. One new first-attempt CPU job is proposed;
the old failed workflow is never rerun. GPU, AWS/S3, real model/data, inference
and training remain outside this plan.

